WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.630
The full-length trailer for the third season
of Stranger Things has finally arrived, showing

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:08.410
our young heroes gearing up for what should
be one of the most memorable summers of their

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.020
lives.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:12.580
And it probably will be, just not for the
reasons they may have hoped.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:17.840
Stranger Things 3 takes place roughly six
months after the events of the second season.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:22.680
The trailer opens with the gang welcoming
Dustin home from camp by way of a little Eleven-assisted

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.180
prank.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:27.660
The trailer doesn't outright say what year
the third season is set in, instead cluing

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:33.110
us in to what time it is with Motley Crue's
1985 hit "Home Sweet Home" playing on Dustin's

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:33.600
boombox.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.380
You can also see the current year on Dustin's
hat.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.580
The name of the camp Dustin's returning from,
"Camp Knowhere," seems like it might be a

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:45.300
reference to a location in the Guardians of
the Galaxy, a franchise with its own nostalgic

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:50.480
ties to the '80s, from a writer-director who's
made his fair share of slimy, Stranger Things-esque

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.480
creature features.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.520
Joining the cast for season 3 is Cary Elwes,
who would hold a special place in the hearts

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:01.070
of certain film fans forever even if he had
never done anything but portray the lovelorn

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.260
Westley in the 1987 classic The Princess Bride.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.060
"As you wish."

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:12.220
Elwes' role isn't so lovable this time around;
he plays Mayor Kline, previously revealed

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:17.000
in promotional materials for Stranger Things
3 as the shady driving force behind the construction

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.220
of the new Starcourt Mall.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.820
Character descriptions from the new season
have described the character as, quote, "handsome,

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:27.710
slick, and sleazy… your classic '80s politician,
more concerned with his own image than with

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.720
the people of the small town he governs."

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.800
So on top of all the other monstrous activity,
it looks like season 3 will have something

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.340
of a political angle at work.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:42.180
Also joining the cast this season is Jake
Busey as Bruce, a writer for the Hawkins Post.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.180
But he's no crusading journalist seeking to
expose Mayor Kline's corruption.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:50.820
His character description pegs him as a man
of questionable morals with a sick sense of

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:51.320
humor.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:55.940
We see only the briefest of shots featuring
the character in the trailer, and he looks

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:56.540
sick, all right.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.700
He appears to be standing in the hall inside
some kind of research facility, most likely

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:06.040
the Hawkins National Laboratory that's connected
to all of the town's interdimensional goings-on.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:11.220
He's unkempt, with his tie undone, smeared
with blood and sporting a twisted smile.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:16.180
His appearance is the first of several clues
which may hint at Hawkins' big problem this

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:16.680
year.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:21.560
There seems to be some kind of infection going
around, one which looks to have also spread

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.980
to Billy Hargrove, everyone's least-favorite
evil step-brother.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:30.760
Lucas' sister Erica was a comedic bright spot
of Stranger Things 2, but her role was a small

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:31.260
one.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.740
This season, we're going to find out a little
more about her, not the least of which is

00:02:35.749 --> 00:02:40.760
the fact that, apparently, the prospect of
coming face-to-face with zombified townspeople

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.819
and horrific, spider-looking monsters doesn't
freak her out in the least.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:49.320
In one shot, she's seen commando-crawling
through an air duct in full Die Hard mode,

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.640
wearing a makeshift miner's helmet made out
of flashlights and tape.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.620
She only appeared in four episodes of the
second season, but it looks like Erica will

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:00.739
be a little closer to the action this time
around, joining her big brother and his friends

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.140
in their unsupervised, monster-fighting activities.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:07.940
Previously released promotional materials
for this season have leaned heavily on cryptic

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:13.169
imagery and phrases, like the line "When blue
and yellow meet in the West", a phrase which

00:03:13.169 --> 00:03:17.239
has turned up in a short teaser trailer and
hidden in Morse code in a behind-the-scenes

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:17.740
book.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:19.640
What could this be referring to?

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.820
There are a of couple possibilities.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.739
One shot in the new trailer features Eleven,
all alone and wearing a yellow shirt, standing

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.860
on the beach as an eerie light illuminates
the night sky.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:34.900
Behind her and to the left is a blue, blue
body of water; could it be that a pivotal

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:35.960
plot point occurs here?

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:40.960
It's also been pointed out that, in the "Starcourt
Mall Announcement" teaser released earlier

00:03:40.969 --> 00:03:46.420
in 2018, the hands of the clock on the mall's
face also happen to be yellow and blue, indicating

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:49.400
that something serious might go down when
the hands "meet."

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:54.749
The season will conclude with an episode entitled
"The Battle of Starcourt," and there's more

00:03:54.749 --> 00:03:58.829
than one shot in the trailer indicating that
Hawkins' new mall is indeed going to be the

00:03:58.829 --> 00:04:00.620
scene of some serious trouble.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:06.299
One shot sees Steve, Dustin, Erica, and newcomer
Robin, a co-worker of Steve's at the food

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:10.240
court ice cream shop, barricaded behind a
set of the mall's sliding doors.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.660
Another shot shows the whole gang battered,
bloody, and looking ready to take on whatever

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.940
adversary has invaded their new shopping center.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:21.959
We also seem to have gotten a bit of clarification
on the title of episode three, "The Case of

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:22.880
the Missing Lifeguard."

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:28.220
An early sequence reveals that Billy has a
new job as a lifeguard at the local pool,

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:31.860
and he exchanges a flirty glance with a cute
co-worker who passes by him.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:37.480
This same girl is seen very briefly in that
closing montage, seemingly being dragged into

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:40.440
the depths of the Upside Down as Billy watches
helplessly.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:44.840
Could this be the incident which leads to
the onset of Billy's unfortunate condition?

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.260
Either way, it looks like the evils of the
Upside Down are once again making an effort

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:53.440
to break through into the real world, and
Eleven seems to once again be the only person

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:54.220
who can stop it.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:58.980
The powerful psychic is shown getting sucked
into the Upside Down, confronting some kind

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:03.650
of force in that shot on the beach, and standing
blindfolded with a slight nosebleed in front

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:08.700
of a freezer chock full of the one thing she's
never been able to resist, Eggo waffles.

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:13.640
But most tellingly, the spot's final moments
see her in that same yellow shirt, face full

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:19.020
of righteous anger, nose bleeding like a faucet,
facing off against that grotesque spider-thing.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:22.040
Let's hope she gets to have at least one Eggo
first.

